# Zero hand-written DDL migrations

Escalite uses **Atlas** with a canonical declarative schema. See doc 08 (`#database-schema-workflow`) and `docs/adr/0001-atlas-declarative-schema.md`.

## Canonical source of truth

| What | Path |
| ---- | ---- |
| Declarative schema | `services/api/schema/` (Atlas HCL) |
| Generated migrations | `services/api/migrations/` (from `atlas migrate diff` only) |
| sqlc queries | `services/api/queries/` |

## Required workflow for schema changes

1. Edit `services/api/schema/` (tables, columns, indexes, constraints).
2. Run `atlas migrate diff --env local` (or `task schema:diff` when defined).
3. Commit **both** schema and generated migration files in the same commit/PR.

## Forbidden

- Hand-writing `CREATE TABLE`, `ALTER TABLE`, `DROP`, indexes, or constraints in `services/api/migrations/`
- Creating migration files manually (no `touch`, no copy-paste DDL into new `.sql` files)
- Using `goose create` or other migration scaffolders for DDL
- Committing schema changes without the matching generated migration
- Editing generated migration DDL to "fix" drift — fix the canonical schema and re-run `atlas migrate diff`

## Allowed

- Hand-written **DML only** (INSERT/UPDATE backfills) in a migration file when paired with an ADR note in the PR — never DDL
- Editing `atlas.hcl` and Taskfile migration tasks
- sqlc query files in `services/api/queries/` (not schema DDL)

## Verifier / orchestrator gate

Schema-related task **FAIL** if committed migration files contain DDL that was not produced by `atlas migrate diff` in the same change set, or if canonical schema and migrations are out of sync.
